0..75 Comment "// A returner\'s row is a row of interfaces: each interface\'s name holds its"
76..152 Comment "// signature, no name twice, the names in no order of their own (#2269). Two"
153..223 Comment "// rows that list the same interfaces in different orders are one row,"
224..302 Comment "// sequencing joins the rows of the computations it runs, and a computation is"
303..373 Comment "// read where a row holding more is asked: the set operations of a row"
374..448 Comment "// (Hillerström and Lindley, \"Liberating Effects with Rows and Handlers\","
449..507 Comment "// Type-Driven Development 2016, § 2). What refuses is in"
508..558 Comment "// `../../pathological/control/effect-rows.gandr`."
560..622 Comment "// `peek` reads through `std.fs.Eff`; `once` states `Partial`."
